menu "PhoneUse: Bluetooth stack"

    config PHONEUSE_BT_KEEP_CLASSIC
        bool "Keep the Classic BT (BR/EDR) controller running (needed for HFP later)"
        default n
        depends on BTDM_CTRL_MODE_BTDM
        help
            Off: the Classic BT controller memory is released at boot and the controller
            runs BLE-only (more free RAM, fewer moving parts) - the right choice while only
            BLE HID is used.
            On: the controller runs in dual mode so a Classic BT profile such as HFP can be
            started next to BLE HID. Also enable CONFIG_BT_CLASSIC_ENABLED and the profile's
            own options; coexistence of BLE HID and HFP has not been validated yet.

endmenu
